# Drafted by Gemini (R17 godlee), edited.

~ common_room
Narrator: Patients sit at neat tables with spoons and no knives, queuing quietly by the pharmacy window. When a man drops his tray, a bare-faced nurse with a painted porcelain eyepatch steps in.
sarah_godlee [neutral]: Take our brother to the dispensary for a second draught, if you please. Good evening, visitors. I am Head Nurse Sarah Godlee.
* Introduce ourselves -> common_intro
* [Insight DC 12] Watch her closely -> common_insight_ok | common_insight_fail
* Ask about the patients -> common_patients
* Leave -> END

~ common_intro
sarah_godlee [neutral]: You are welcome at Memory's Rest so long as you mind the plaques on the walls. Keep your voices low, do not pester the residents about old times, and stay belowstairs.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: Strict house manners. The air smells of fear and cheap starch.
-> common_room

~ common_insight_ok
Narrator: Her tone never rises, yet the patient who dropped his tray is trembling at the word dispensary. Beneath the starched courtesy lies a cold and practiced hand.
set mr_godlee_read
-> common_room

~ common_insight_fail
Narrator: She adjusts her cuffs without a crease out of place, every inch the tireless ward sister keeping a fragile house in order.
-> common_room

~ common_patients
sarah_godlee [smile]: They are mended, quiet, and spared the weight of whatever brought them across the water. That is the Matron's gift to them, and my charge to protect.
-> common_room

~ quarters
Narrator: Godlee's room smells of starch and black irises arranged in a tall glass vase. Ledgers sit squared on the desk beside a narrow, spotless bed.
sarah_godlee [weary]: Close the door behind you. You have the look of people who notice more than is good for them, and I have a concern regarding the Matron.
* [Persuasion DC 17] Win her trust -> trust_ok | trust_fail
* [Deception DC 17] Tell her we share her worry -> trust_ok | trust_fail
* [if flag.mr_has_memento] Show her a memento of Marius -> trust_proof
* [if flag.godlee_trust and quest.godlees_mementos == asked] Give her our answer about the mementos -> wish
* Look for her diary -> diary_search
* Leave -> END

~ trust_ok
sarah_godlee [sad]: She cures everyone in this house except herself. Upstairs in her private chambers she keeps relics of her late husband, and every glance at them bleeds her dry.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Even the headliner weeps backstage, darling, and her nurse looks eager to snip the threads.
set godlee_trust
quest godlees_mementos asked
-> wish

~ trust_fail
sarah_godlee [neutral]: Perhaps I misjudged your discretion. The hour is late, and you would do well to return to the guest rooms below.
-> quarters

~ trust_proof
sarah_godlee [angry]: Where did you get that? That dead man's trinkets are a sickness in her rooms upstairs, binding her to a grief she ought to have shed years ago.
set godlee_trust
quest godlees_mementos asked
-> wish

~ wish
sarah_godlee [neutral]: Go up to the Matron's quarters and destroy every keepsake of Sir Marius you find. Free her from him, and I will see that the orderlies look the other way.
* Agree to destroy them -> destroy
* [Deception DC 15] Agree, and keep them -> keep_lie | caught
* [ends:godlees_mementos] Refuse -> refuse
* We need time to think -> END

~ destroy
approve delphine_ravelle -3 tobin_hayward -2 rook_coldwake -2: You agreed to destroy the Matron's keepsakes of her dead husband
sarah_godlee [smile]: Good. Burn them or break them, so long as nothing remains to wound her. The ward staff will not trouble your steps tonight.
set godlee_mementos_destroyed
if item:mr_memento_portrait
take mr_memento_portrait
endif
if item:mr_memento_tabard
take mr_memento_tabard
endif
if item:mr_memento_sonnet
take mr_memento_sonnet
endif
set lethica_mementos_carried = 0
set mr_has_memento = 0
quest godlees_mementos destroyed
-> END

~ keep_lie
approve silas_vane +3 delphine_ravelle +2 rook_coldwake -1: You bluffed Nurse Godlee and kept the Matron's mementos
sarah_godlee [neutral]: See that it is done swiftly and without a trace. I will keep the orderlies occupied on the lower landing.
quest godlees_mementos kept
set godlee_lied_to
-> END

~ caught
sarah_godlee [angry]: Do not lie to my face in my own ward. Leave this room at once before I have the orderlies escort you from the island.
* [ends:godlees_mementos] Insist she is wrong -> caught_end
* Confess, and agree to destroy them after all -> destroy

~ caught_end
quest godlees_mementos caught
set mr_staff_hostile
-> END

~ refuse
approve rook_coldwake +2 lucan_houndstooth +2 silas_vane -1: You refused Nurse Godlee's demand to destroy the dead knight's relics
sarah_godlee [neutral]: Then we have nothing further to discuss. Mind the house rules while you remain under our roof.
quest godlees_mementos refused
-> END

~ diary_search
Narrator: The narrow bed is made with hospital corners, its hem hanging just above the scrubbed floorboards.
* [Perception DC 14] Search under the bed -> diary_found | diary_miss
* Step back from the bed -> quarters

~ diary_found
Narrator: Tucked into the slats beneath the mattress is a leather journal filled with cramped devotion to Lethica, and a note on opening the laboratory by injecting a full dose of serum into the carved owl's eye.
give mr_godlee_diary
set mr_lab_open_known
set mr_truth_clues += 1
if flag.mr_truth_clues >= 2 and (quest.all_is_well == find_the_cousin or quest.all_is_well == sign_in)
if not quest.all_is_well >= the_truth
quest all_is_well the_truth
endif
endif
-> quarters

~ diary_miss
Narrator: Your fingers find nothing under the frame save tucked linen and cold floorboards.
-> quarters
